// The words of carbon's twins room ("A diamond and a pencil: twins?"), in English, European Portuguese,
// Polish and German, kid (Explorer) and sci (Scientist). The picture's own story stays in
// src/content/boards/C.js (the easel shows it); the room tells where each twin comes from.
// Sources: diamond ages, depths and kimberlite speeds as Wikipedia's "Diamond" gives them (1 to 3.5 billion
// years, 150 to 250 km, 4 to 20 m/s); graphitised diamonds of Beni Bousera (Pearson and others, Nature
// 1989); Borrowdale (found in the 1500s, the only large deposit of solid graphite) and Conté (1795) as
// Wikipedia's "Pencil"; lead compositions from the CATAS study (HB about two parts graphite to one of clay).
